1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,734
Good Together is a charity event website for the Gold Coast.

2
00:00:04,734 --> 00:00:09,898
This local demonstration covers event discovery, registration,
and the staff management workflow.

3
00:00:09,898 --> 00:00:15,923
The home page retrieves events from a Node and Express API
connected to MySQL.

4
00:00:15,923 --> 00:00:19,365
The cards show current and upcoming public events.

5
00:00:19,365 --> 00:00:23,239
Past and suspended events are excluded from this listing.

6
00:00:23,239 --> 00:00:27,112
Category shortcuts take visitors directly to a filtered search.

7
00:00:27,112 --> 00:00:32,706
The existing Assessment Two design has been extended with
persistent registration and administration.

8
00:00:32,706 --> 00:00:37,010
All people and contact information in this demonstration are
fictional.

9
00:00:37,010 --> 00:00:43,034
The final hosting checks will be carried out separately on each
student's SCU account.

10
00:00:45,640 --> 00:00:49,533
The search page combines a start date, suburb and category.

11
00:00:49,533 --> 00:00:54,204
Here the suburb Southport and the Fun run category narrow the
results.

12
00:00:54,204 --> 00:00:59,654
The browser sends these choices in the query string, so the URL
can be

13
00:00:59,654 --> 00:01:02,768
shared and browser history can restore the filters.

14
00:01:02,768 --> 00:01:08,218
On the server, the conditions are joined together and their
values are bound as

15
00:01:08,218 --> 00:01:09,386
prepared statement parameters.

16
00:01:09,386 --> 00:01:12,890
Clearing filters resets both the form and the results.

17
00:01:12,890 --> 00:01:16,783
A suburb with no matches produces a useful empty state.

18
00:01:16,783 --> 00:01:21,454
Invalid dates and identifiers receive validation messages
instead of a failed page.

19
00:01:21,454 --> 00:01:25,347
Loading, retry and error states are handled through DOM updates.

20
00:01:28,280 --> 00:01:34,611
The event page loads its details and all associated public
registrations through the API.

21
00:01:34,611 --> 00:01:40,490
Registrations are ordered by registration time, newest first,
with the identifier breaking ties.

22
00:01:40,490 --> 00:01:46,821
Names, ticket quantities and dates appear publicly; contact
details are omitted from this list.

23
00:01:46,821 --> 00:01:53,153
Selecting three tickets updates the displayed total, and
Register opens a dedicated page for

24
00:01:53,153 --> 00:01:54,057
this event.

25
00:01:54,057 --> 00:01:58,579
The page shows the event date, venue, organiser and price.

26
00:01:58,579 --> 00:02:03,102
The visitor enters a name, email address and contact phone.

27
00:02:03,102 --> 00:02:07,172
Required fields and contact formats are checked before
submission.

28
00:02:07,172 --> 00:02:13,503
The server checks them again, obtains the ticket price and
current time itself, and

29
00:02:13,503 --> 00:02:14,859
saves the registration.

30
00:02:17,640 --> 00:02:21,508
The confirmation identifies the saved registration and the
ticket total.

31
00:02:21,508 --> 00:02:24,602
No online payment is processed by this application.

32
00:02:24,602 --> 00:02:30,017
Returning to the event shows the new attendee at the top of the
list.

33
00:02:30,017 --> 00:02:34,271
Refreshing still shows the registration because it is stored in
MySQL.

34
00:02:34,271 --> 00:02:39,686
The same email address cannot register for this event a second
time, even if

35
00:02:39,686 --> 00:02:41,233
the letter case changes.

36
00:02:41,233 --> 00:02:44,328
The same person may register for another event.

37
00:02:44,328 --> 00:02:49,743
An email and event pair is protected by a unique database index,
rather than

38
00:02:49,743 --> 00:02:51,676
relying only on the browser.

39
00:02:51,676 --> 00:02:57,091
Events that have ended cannot receive new registrations, and
suspended events are unavailable publicly.

40
00:02:59,800 --> 00:03:05,985
The staff website has consistent navigation to Events, New
event, Categories and the public

41
00:03:05,985 --> 00:03:06,427
site.

42
00:03:06,427 --> 00:03:11,286
Its list includes every event, including active, past and
suspended records.

43
00:03:11,286 --> 00:03:16,146
Staff can use the status filter to focus on one group.

44
00:03:16,146 --> 00:03:22,331
Editing an event retrieves its existing values, together with
the full registration list and

45
00:03:22,331 --> 00:03:23,215
contact details.

46
00:03:23,215 --> 00:03:28,958
Past is calculated from the end time, while suspended is a
publication choice.

47
00:03:28,958 --> 00:03:35,143
The brief allows this teaching version to omit authentication,
so it should use fictional

48
00:03:35,143 --> 00:03:36,026
data only.

49
00:03:36,026 --> 00:03:42,211
A production service would need staff authentication and access
controls before collecting real personal

50
00:03:42,211 --> 00:03:42,653
information.

51
00:03:45,120 --> 00:03:50,022
The new event form validates required descriptions, dates,
amounts and category choices.

52
00:03:50,022 --> 00:03:55,740
Save sends a JSON request to the creation endpoint and returns
the stored identifier.

53
00:03:55,740 --> 00:04:00,642
The same form then edits that record with a full update request.

54
00:04:00,642 --> 00:04:05,544
Suspending the event removes it from public discovery while
retaining its records.

55
00:04:05,544 --> 00:04:09,629
Deleting an event asks for confirmation and calls the API.

56
00:04:09,629 --> 00:04:15,347
An event with registrations is refused with a clear explanation,
so it can be

57
00:04:15,347 --> 00:04:16,164
suspended instead.

58
00:04:16,164 --> 00:04:18,615
An unused event can be deleted.

59
00:04:18,615 --> 00:04:24,334
The category screen also supports creation, editing and
deletion, and prevents deletion of a

60
00:04:24,334 --> 00:04:27,602
category that is still used by an event.

61
00:04:30,640 --> 00:04:34,632
The database contains organisations, categories, events and
registrations.

62
00:04:34,632 --> 00:04:41,618
Registrations reference events through a foreign key and store
attendee details, ticket quantity, a

63
00:04:41,618 --> 00:04:44,612
unit price snapshot and registration time.

64
00:04:44,612 --> 00:04:49,103
Twelve fictional registrations are included in the initial SQL.

65
00:04:49,103 --> 00:04:53,095
The unique event and email index prevents duplicates.

66
00:04:53,095 --> 00:04:56,588
The restricted foreign key prevents orphaned registrations.

67
00:04:56,588 --> 00:05:03,574
The registration API starts a transaction and locks the event
row before checking availability

68
00:05:03,574 --> 00:05:05,570
and inserting the record.

69
00:05:05,570 --> 00:05:09,063
Updates and deletion take the same lock.

70
00:05:09,063 --> 00:05:11,059
This coordinates concurrent changes.

71
00:05:11,059 --> 00:05:18,045
The integration tests exercise both duplicate submissions and
registration against deletion, using a real

72
00:05:18,045 --> 00:05:19,542
isolated MySQL database.

73
00:05:22,000 --> 00:05:26,751
The client uses plain JavaScript modules, fetch and async
functions.

74
00:05:26,751 --> 00:05:31,502
API responses are rendered using text content and DOM elements.

75
00:05:31,502 --> 00:05:36,253
The staff forms send JSON and show server validation errors.

76
00:05:36,253 --> 00:05:41,954
Weather is an optional server-side call to Open Meteo using
event coordinates.

77
00:05:41,954 --> 00:05:46,230
The interface shows conditions and daily temperatures when
available.

78
00:05:46,230 --> 00:05:52,882
Dates beyond the sixteen day forecast window, missing
coordinates and network failures produce an

79
00:05:52,882 --> 00:05:54,782
explanation without blocking registration.

80
00:05:54,782 --> 00:06:01,434
Seventy-one backend tests and forty-six browser checks passed
locally, including Chromium and WebKit at

81
00:06:01,434 --> 00:06:03,809
mobile, tablet and desktop widths.

82
00:06:03,809 --> 00:06:07,610
The source packages and deployment guide are prepared.

83
00:06:07,610 --> 00:06:14,262
Both SCU deployments, the final OneDrive share link and
individual contribution explanations remain to

84
00:06:14,262 --> 00:06:16,637
be completed before assessment submission.
